-- title:
--   Membership in (varpi) versus substitution by varpi
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, let $j_0 : \mathrm{Zp2}\,q \to k$ be a ring homomorphism from the Witt vectors of the field with $q^2$ elements, and let $X_0$ be a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $k$ relative to $j_0$: a two-dimensional commutative formal group law $F = X_0.F$ over $k$ together with series $\mathrm{act}(a)$ ($a \in \mathrm{Zp2}\,q$) and $\varpi = X_0.\varpi$, all endomorphisms of $F$, with $\mathrm{act}$ multiplicative and additive, $\varpi \circ \varpi = \mathrm{act}(q)$ and $\varpi \circ \mathrm{act}(a) = \mathrm{act}(\mathrm{Frob}\,a) \circ \varpi$, such that the submodules `lieZero` $j_0$ and `lieOne` $j_0$ are complementary and invertible over $k$, and such that $\mathrm{act}(q)$ satisfies `HasKernelOfDegree` with degree $q^4$. Write $\partial_F h = h(F(X,Y)) - h(X) - h(Y)$ for the additive coboundary, and $[q]_F = X_0.F.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,q$ for the $q$-th iterated addition series of $F$ (defined by $[0]_F = 0$ and $[n+1]_F(X) = [n]_F(X) +_F X$). Two assertions are made about $k[[X_1,X_2]] =$ `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k`. First: if $h$ has zero constant term, $\partial_F h$ lies in the ideal of $k[[X_1,X_2,Y_1,Y_2]]$ generated by the four series $\varpi_l(X)$, $\varpi_l(Y)$, and $h \circ \varpi$ lies in the ideal generated by the components of $[q]_F$, then $h$ lies in the ideal generated by the components of $\varpi$. Second: if $g$ has zero constant term, $\partial_F g$ lies in the ideal generated by the four series $[q]_F(X)$, $[q]_F(Y)$, and $g$ lies in the ideal generated by the components of $\varpi$, then there is an $h$ with zero constant term such that $\partial_F h$ lies in the ideal generated by $\varpi(X)$, $\varpi(Y)$ and $g - h\circ\varpi$ lies in the ideal generated by the components of $[q]_F$.
--
--   In the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, this is the power-series form of the exactness of $0 \to \mathrm{Hom}(X_0[\varpi],\mathbb G_a) \xrightarrow{\varpi^*} \mathrm{Hom}(X_0[q],\mathbb G_a) \to \mathrm{Hom}(X_0[\varpi],\mathbb G_a)$ coming from $\varpi^2 = [q]$: injectivity of $\varpi^*$ on the level of ideals, and descent of a primitive modulo $[q]_F$ along $\varpi$. It feeds the analysis of primitives modulo $[q]_F$ in `exists_primitives_mod_nthSeries_typed_lines_of_finrank_eq_two`, and its proof uses the finite flatness of substitution by $\varpi$ together with the computation $\dim_k k[[X_1,X_2]]/(\varpi) = q^2$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_SpecialFormalODModule_mem_span_varpi_of_subst_varpi_mem_and_exists_subst_varpi_of_mem_span_varpi.lean

